      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don't think this is a good idea in limited contexts, but a more functional safety and performance system would be useful. Add the option to specify performance limits by safety ranking, as well as set a hard \"limit\" on how many \"very poor\" avatars can display at one time.\nSome of the \"performance blocked\" avatars I've seen aren't actually that bad or cause any issues on my end. It feels more like they're performance blocked for \"technical\" reasons (exceeding some kind of limit, without regards to the actual performance hit.). Whereas others are entirely awful and should not exist.\nTBH if there was a way to test Quest avatars ON Quest before upload, if they exceed a certain limit, to measure performance, that'd also be useful.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
