      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just a heads up: VRCSDK version 3 avatars can have toggleable props and other accessories that are including in the Avatar Ranking System, even if they cannot be all shown at once, or are unlikely to.\nSince getting into avatar creating, my base avatar is under 20K poly. But I have an optional clothing piece, which bumps the number up by about 2K, and props I can spawn in either hand, another 3K each (after optimization), plus an emote prop, that is about 400.\nThis puts my total at around 29K, 9K over the \"very poor\" restriction, but my avatar actually performs, on average, as a \"Poor\", or (realistically, on Quest 2,) a \"Medium\" avatar.\nVRChat's Ranking System is not designed for nor around SDK3 restrictions, and so \"Very Poor\" can be anything from \"a Medium Model with optional props\", and \"a 60K+ poly avatar with 40 materials\".\nSo to double down on my previous comment, **not only is this a bad idea, but it would discourage avatar makers from bringing their avatars to quest**.\nNot to mention the fact that the ranking system is designed **around the Quest 1**. The Quest 2 can handle more than the Quest 1 can, but the Avatar Ranking System does not take this into account.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
